e-supply-chain-risk walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the vendor risk assessment authored and self-reviewed in-session
against NIST SP 800-161 Rev. 1 (PDF fetched 2026-10-10, 4,845,469 bytes;
327 pages; TOC verified: ch.2 enterprise-wide risk management incl. 2.3
multilevel risk management and 2.3.5 C-SCRM PMO; ch.3 Critical Success Factors
incl. 3.1 C-SCRM in Acquisition, 3.2 information sharing, 3.3 training and
awareness, 3.4 key practices).

Status note recorded honestly in-lesson: Rev. 1 (May 2022) was withdrawn from
its old nvlpubs URL on 2024-11-01; the same Rev. 1 is the current edition on
csrc.nist.gov (verified on the csrc publication page 2026-10-10).

Scope: fictional Harbor Clinic buying a cloud billing platform (patient contact
data + payment tokens, EHR API integration, 40-person vendor, SOC 2 Type II).
Six factors assessed w/ ratings+reasons: access (high), criticality (high),
posture evidence (medium — auditor exceptions read), fourth parties (medium),
exit (high risk — CSV-only export, 90-day auto-renew, no deletion attestation),
provenance (low/noted). Mitigations: minimum-requirements clause, 48h vendor
breach notification, 30-day subprocessor-change notice w/ right to object,
data return + deletion attestation, least-privilege API scoping, annual +
trigger-based reassessment. Decision: conditional accept — owner: operations
director; review: 12 months or on trigger; accepted residual risks named.

